# Frosthollow (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 3): mining and snow, a high valley in the Whitefangs. Short, dry, dark
# humour; everything is rock, seam, lamp and cold. Drafts (phase 3), to be written properly with you (phase 7).

grammar frosthollow
greet = Warm hearth | Hearth to you
greet.broad = 'Arth | 'Arth and lamp
farewell = Keep your lamp lit | Lamp lit
agree = Sound as rock | Aye, sound
refuse = Dead seam, that | Not a chance
surprise = Well, strike me | Cold iron
annoyed = Slag and ashes | Cave it all
very = deep
good = sound | solid
bad = cracked | dead
worthless = dead rock | slag
luck = a good seam
child = whelp
pet!! = old stone | lamp of mine
money = brass
cold = cold | biting | iron-cold
tired = spent | done in
nonsense = slag | fool's gold
tag = , eh
tag.broad = , eh, eh
oath! = Black seam | Cold iron | Lamp and pick
home = my own hearth
